<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Bapheus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1301</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-ottoman-wars">Byzantine–Ottoman wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Bapheus was fought in 1301 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicomedia">Nicomedia</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> between the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osman-i">Osman I</a> and a Byzantine army. Osman's victory brought him prestige and attracted followers to his principality. It is regarded as a key event in the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-bapheus.jpg" alt="Battle of Bapheus" width="320" height="145" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kocaeli_Turkey_Provinces_locator.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
